    "Immediate-release nifedipine should not be administered to patients with NSTE-ACS in the absence of beta-blocker therapy. This is because CCBs like dihydropyridines may worsen outcomes without beta-blockers. CCBs such as verapamil and diltiazem may reduce reinfarction in some studies but are not always effective. Verapamil may benefit hypertensive patients without LV dysfunction after AMI. Ranolazine is recommended for treating chronic angina and showed a reduction in cardiovascular events. IABP counterpulsation might be used for high-risk patients with severe ACS events. High-intensity statin therapy is recommended for managing cholesterol in NSTE-ACS patients.": "genes",
